    "text_delta": "ess of formalizing rejection feedback often moves to the bottom of the priority queue.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Recommended Next Steps\n\n1. **Follow up constructively:**\n   Instead of asking for a formal written dossier, send a brief, courteous follow-up asking if the hiring manager or HR partner would have 10–15 minutes for a brief phone conversation. People are far more willing to share candid, constructive feedback verbally than in writing.\n   > *\"Thank you again for the opportunity to interview for the Head of Risk Modelling role. I understand the team has likely been busy finalizing the hire. As I look toward future leadership opportunities, I would greatly appreciate 10 minutes by phone for any constructive feedback on where I can strengthen my candidacy for similar roles.\"*\n\n2. **Conduct an honest self-assessment:**\n   Reflect on your interview discussions: Did the conversation lean too heavily into technical/statistical details rather than regulatory strategy, stakeholder communication, and team leadership? \n\n3. **Recognize your positioning:**\n   Reaching the final three for a senior executive position confirms that your profile and qualifications are highly competitive. With minor adjustments to emphasize regulatory strategy and executive leadership alongside your quantitative strengths, you are well-positioned for the next leadership opening.\n",
